% Takeaway: real label noise comes from many sources and is not independent, identically distributed or Gaussian.
% Takeaway: label noise is not always harmful; it can act as regularisation.
% Paragraph 2: the shape of real noise is not Gaussian.
% - Studies of noise robustness usually add independent, zero-mean Gaussian error to labels.
% - \citet{Kruger2012} rejected normality of repeat bioactivity differences and fitted a Laplace distribution.
